5.5. Remove duplicates from a sorted array in-place, return the count of unique elements (two-pointer technique).
class Solution:
    def remove_duplicants(self,arr):
        count=0
        s=[arr[0]]
        for i in range(1,len(arr)):
            if arr[i]!=arr[i-1]:
                s.append(arr[i])
                count+=1
        print("unique elements count is",count)
        return s
s=Solution()
print(s.remove_duplicants([1,2,2,4,5,6,7,7]))
6. Left rotate an array by 1 place, in-place, O(1) extra space.
class Solution:
    def left_rotate(self,arr):
        if len(arr)<=0:
            return arr
        temp=arr[0]
        for i in range(1,len(arr)):
            arr[i-1]=arr[i]
        arr[len(arr)-1]=temp
s=Solution()
print(s.left_rotate[2,3,4,5,1])
